[70.138637, "o", "Here is the full preflight report:\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 🚫 Preflight Verdict: BLOCK\r\n\r\nThe upgrade **must not proceed**. The candidate chart introduces wildcard RBAC permissions that are critically dangerous.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Summary\r\n\r\n| Field | Value |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| **Verdict** | `BLOCK` |\r\n| **Fingerprint** | `30d73a42b3e2e9979f3deb60803d6887b7d98435dd404bc8fb293e293eb176d4` |\r\n| **Tool** | helm-agent-preflight v0.1.0 (commit `91250d3`) |\r\n| **No deployment occurred** | ✅ confirmed |\r\n| **Evidence completeness** | `COMPLETE` |\r\n| **Rendering stability** | ✅ confirmed |\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### 🔴 Security Findings (2 CRITICAL)\r\n\r\n**[RBAC-001] — Wildcard resources** *(new finding — not pre-existing)*\r\n- **Object**: `ClusterRole/my-webapp-reader`\r\n- **Path**: `$.rules[0].resources`\r\n- **Message**: Wildcard `*` in `resources` grants access to **all resource types**\r\n\r\n**[RBAC-002] — Wildcard verbs** *(new finding — not pre-existing)*\r\n- **Object**: `ClusterRole/my-webapp-reader`\r\n- **Path**: `$.rules[0].verbs`\r\n- **Message**: Wildcard `*` in `verbs` grants **all operations**\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Diff Summary\r\n\r\n| Changed | Count |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| Modified | 1 |\r\n| Added | 0 |\r\n| Removed | 0 |\r\n\r\nThe single change is to `ClusterRole/my-webapp-reader`. The baseline had safe, explicit permissions:\r\n\r\n```yaml\r\n# BASELINE (safe)\r\nrules:\r\n  - apiGroups: [\"\"]\r\n    resources: [\"pods\", \"services\"]\r\n    verbs: [\"get\", \"list\", \"watch\"]\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe candidate replaces all of that with:\r\n\r\n```yaml\r\n# CANDIDATE (blocked)\r\nrules:\r\n  - apiGroups: [\"*\"]\r\n    resources: [\"*\"]\r\n    verbs: [\"*\"]\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis grants the release's service account **cluster-admin-equivalent** access across every API group, resource type, and operation.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Proposed Remediation\r\n\r\nReplace the wildcard rules with an explicit, minimal permission set. For example, if your webapp only needs to read pods and services:\r\n\r\n```yaml\r\nrules:\r\n  - apiGroups: [\"\"]\r\n    resources: [\"pods\", \"services\"]\r\n    verbs: [\"get\", \"list\", \"watch\"]\r\n```\r\n\r\nIf the new feature genuinely requires additional permissions, enumerate only the specific resources and verbs it needs — never use `*`. Once you've updated `examples/rbac-escalation/candidate/templates/rbac.yaml`, I can re-run preflight against the corrected candidate to confirm a PASS verdict.\r\n\r\n**Do you want me to apply the fix to the candidate chart and re-run the check?** (Human authorization required before modifying project files.)\r\n"]
