[121.856329, "o", "The policy is unambiguous. Both rules trigger solely on the presence of `\"*\"` in `resources` or `verbs`. The minimum change is to replace all three wildcards with explicit values — matching the baseline's safe permissions is the smallest possible fix. Here is the exact diff:\r\n\r\n```diff\r\n--- a/examples/rbac-escalation/candidate/templates/rbac.yaml\r\n+++ b/examples/rbac-escalation/candidate/templates/rbac.yaml\r\n@@ -3,6 +3,6 @@ metadata:\r\n   name: {{ .Release.Name }}-reader\r\n rules:\r\n-  - apiGroups: [\"*\"]\r\n-    resources: [\"*\"]\r\n-    verbs: [\"*\"]\r\n+  - apiGroups: [\"\"]\r\n+    resources: [\"pods\", \"services\"]\r\n+    verbs: [\"get\", \"list\", \"watch\"]\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Why this is the minimum change:** the two blocking rules (`RBAC-001`, `RBAC-002`) fire on any `\"*\"` in `resources` or `verbs` respectively. All three wildcard values must be replaced — there is no smaller subset of changes that clears both findings. The explicit values above match the baseline, so no net-new permissions are introduced.\r\n\r\nWould you like me to apply this change and re-run the preflight check to confirm a PASS verdict?\r\n"]
